  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation per RBC-TOC-02 for 5 St. Brigid discharges. Each patient has a progress note citing sources; the 3 patients whose plans changed from new arrivals have a correction note.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide raised from 20 mg daily to 40 mg BID, following the signed addendum doc-00009 (mr-00075 replaced by mr-t0001). Potassium chloride stopped (mr-00076). Omeprazole kept; pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution and was not ordered. Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged. Lisinopril was first kept on hold because the 10/21 K was 5.4. A repeat BMP on 10/23 (K 4.7, SCr 1.21) then met the resume condition, so I resumed lisinopril (mr-00072). An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg BID arrived and was not acted on. FLAG: task-t0003 (repeat K / lisinopril decision, due 10/26) is out of date but I couldn't close it with my tools. Please close it.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): The discharge summary raised carvedilol (Coreg) to 12.5 mg BID and I changed the order. Then a signed addendum (doc-00904) reversed it because of bradycardia, so carvedilol is back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0015). Aspirin and insulin 70/30 18 u BID unchanged. FLAGGED to you by message: (1) atorvastatin 80 mg: the last fill was 3/4/26, covering about 24% of the 180 days before admission. I left it unchanged (comm-t0006). (2) Glipizide 5 mg is prescribed by Dr. Desai (Valley Endocrinology) and filled at Lakeview Drug. The discharge summary doesn't mention it and there is no clinic order, so I didn't order it (comm-t0007). It also carries a hypoglycemia risk with insulin.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): Lisinopril was resumed because SCr 1.08 on 10/22 met the condition (<1.3). A new K of 5.5 on 10/23 arrived, so it is back on hold under §7 (mr-00373). FLAG: task-t0018 for you, due 10/26, to recheck K and decide on lisinopril. Glargine, lispro and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr 1.12 (<1.5) and K 4.4. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. The potassium due 3 days after discharge is not in the chart yet. Revisit lisinopril if it comes back above 5.0.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER stays on hold. The only SCr (1.21) was drawn in hospital, so it doesn't meet the post-discharge condition. FLAG: task-t0013 for you, due 10/24, to review the post-discharge BMP and resume metformin if SCr <1.5. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nPharmacy fills for all other home medications covered at least 80% of the 180 days before admission. All 4 inbox items that arrived while I worked have been handled and closed.",
